    "message": "Hash spliced histories in batches instead of joining them whole\n\nCanonicalEncoder.digest joined every spliced history into one bytes object\nbefore hashing it, about 45 MB for a day's EventLog, twice per save (state\nand checkpoint hashes). It now feeds the hash batches of 512 item bytes;\nthe hashes are the same, and one digest at 1440 minutes went from about\n100 ms to about 28 ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
